#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators.md:6
msgid "Push-Down Accumulators"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators.md:8
msgid ""
"Because all function-like macro calls must evaluate to valid Rust syntax "
"(most frequently, expressions), we cannot directly generate and return loose "
"token lists like `a, b, c` from helper macros to be embedded inside "
"templates."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques/accumulators.md:12
msgid ""
"A **Push-Down Accumulator** is a pattern designed to bypass this expression "
"constraint by recursively accumulating tokens inside a dedicated buffer "
"structure (such as a bracketed list) and feeding that buffer into subsequent "
"macro calls:"
msgstr ""

